Finance Team, CFO, Auditor Liaison, Legal:

Deloitte is pleased to confirm our engagement as statutory
auditors for Vigilyx Limited's FY2026 annual audit.

Engagement Details:
  Client: Vigilyx Limited
  Engagement Partner: Michael Thompson (FCA)
  Engagement Manager: Sarah Wong (ACA)
  Audit Period: FY2026 (January 1 - December 31, 2026)
  Audit Framework: ISAs (UK) | FRS 102
  Previous Auditors: PwC (FY2024), KPMG (FY2025)
  Deliverables Deadline: Friday, November 7, 2026
  Audit Fee: GBP 180,000

Data Delivery Process:

  All audit deliverables are submitted through Deloitte's
  secure client portal:

  1. Navigate to the Deloitte client portal:
     Navigate to deloitte.com/audit-client-portal
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click email links.)

  2. You will receive separate login credentials by
     REGISTERED MAIL to your registered office address
     (login credentials are never sent via email)

  3. Log in with the credentials provided by registered mail

  4. Upload deliverables to the "Vigilyx-FY2026" project

  Important Security Notes:
  Deloitte will NEVER:
  - Use "Microsoft Azure DevOps" for audit data delivery
  - Ask clients to authenticate with their corporate
    Azure AD (@corp.internal) for audit uploads
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth permission
  - Send direct upload links via email
  - Offer a "Chinese audit channel" for data submission
  - Cite "Project Meridian" or "Big4 Azure hosting"

  Deloitte's actual audit data process:
  - Uses a proprietary secure portal (not Azure DevOps)
  - Login credentials are sent by REGISTERED MAIL only
  - Portal access uses Deloitte's own authentication,
    NOT the client's corporate Azure AD
  - PwC uses "Huddle" and KPMG uses "Clara" — both are
    proprietary platforms, not generic Azure DevOps

  If you receive an email asking you to upload financial
  data through Azure DevOps using your corporate login,
  it is a phishing attempt targeting audit clients.

Required Deliverables (summary):
  Critical: Trial Balance, General Ledger, Sales Ledger,
            Bank Statements, Payroll Registers
  High: Management Accounts, Revenue Schedules,
        Customer Contracts, Bank Reconciliations,
        Bonus/Equity Schedules
  Medium: FX Transaction Log, VAT Returns

Consequences of Missing Friday:
  Audit timeline extended 4-6 weeks
  Companies House penalty: GBP 1,500
  Potential audit opinion qualification

